### Message Passing Interface (MPI)
# Many programs (Relion, Xmipp, ...) use MPI. The MPI stack used at run time
# must be ONE self-consistent set: mpirun + core libs + PMIx plugins that all
# match each other. Pick ONE strategy below by (un)commenting.
#
#   BLOCK A (ACTIVE, default) — use the container's OWN OpenMPI.
#     Correct for workstations and any SINGLE-NODE run (incl. single-node
#     multi-GPU). Nothing MPI-related is bound from the host, so the container's
#     mpirun, libs and PMIx components stay matched. This is also what avoids the
#     crash:  mca_pmix_ext3x.so: undefined symbol: PMIx_Info_create  (exit 127)
#     -- that was caused by the OLD config partially overwriting the container's
#     MPI with host files (an incompatible mix of host plugins + container libpmix).
#
#   BLOCK B (commented) — use the HOST / cluster OpenMPI.
#     Needed ONLY for MULTI-NODE MPI, where the container must use the cluster's
#     process launcher / interconnect. Two HARD requirements:
#       1) Generation match: the host OpenMPI must match the one the container's
#          RELION was built against (4.x vs 5.x). Check: mpirun --version.
#       2) Mount points must be creatable: binding a host file whose path does
#          NOT already exist inside the (read-only) image fails with
#          "destination ... doesn't exist in container" -- exactly the error you
#          hit for /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libpmix.so.2. Fix by enabling
#          Apptainer overlay/underlay (admin: `enable underlay = yes`, or run
#          with `--underlay`), or by binding only paths that already exist in
#          the image.

# ======================= BLOCK A: container's own MPI ======================
# (workstation / single node) -- recommended default. /tmp is bound for MPI's
# shared-memory session files.
SCIPMPI_CMD=" --bind /tmp "

# ================= BLOCK B: host / cluster MPI (multi-node) ================
# To use: comment out BLOCK A's SCIPMPI_CMD above, then uncomment this block.
# CLUSTER_MPI_PREFIX: root of the host/cluster OpenMPI installation.
#   - Ubuntu/Debian system OpenMPI (apt):          /usr
#   - Environment-module / spack / source build:   e.g. /opt/openmpi-5.0.6
